<title>FRANCE: Thomson should remain public - Socialists.</title>
<headline>Thomson should remain public - Socialists.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-owned electronics company Thomson SA should remain a public company and should not be split into two units, the French Socialist party said on Friday.</p>
<p>In a statement, Socialist Christian Bataille said, &quot;Thomson must remain a public company.&quot;</p>
<p>The government plans to privatise Thomson in two parts, first selling its profitable defence arm Thomson-CSF and the money-losing consumer electronics division Thomson Multimedia.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
